%% Campaign Revision Sequence Diagram
%% Also illustrates the reconciled stale-approval scenario.
%% Traces to: docs/02-solution-design/LLD/workflow-state-machine.md (Reconciling the Stale-Approval Scenario)

%%{init: {'theme':'base', 'themeVariables': {'primaryColor':'#eef2f7','primaryBorderColor':'#0b2340','primaryTextColor':'#0b2340','lineColor':'#0b2340','secondaryColor':'#dde6f0','tertiaryColor':'#ffffff','fontFamily':'Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif','actorFontSize':'15px','noteFontSize':'14px','messageFontSize':'14px'}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
    actor Marketer
    actor Reviewer
    participant Submit as SubmitCampaign
    participant Withdraw as WithdrawSubmission
    participant Revise as ReviseCampaign
    participant Review as ReviewCampaign
    participant Repo as CampaignRepository

    Marketer->>Submit: execute(campaignId)
    Submit->>Repo: save(campaign, v1, state=pendingReview)
    Note over Reviewer: Reviewer opens v1 in their UI (no decision yet)

    Marketer->>Withdraw: execute(campaignId)
    Withdraw->>Repo: load(campaignId)
    Repo-->>Withdraw: Campaign(v1, pendingReview, no ApprovalRecord)
    Withdraw->>Repo: save(campaign, state=draft)

    Marketer->>Revise: execute(campaignId, newSnapshot)
    Revise->>Repo: load(campaignId)
    Revise->>Repo: save(campaign, v2, state=pendingReview)

    Note over Reviewer: Reviewer, unaware of the withdraw/resubmit, still holds v1

    Reviewer->>Review: execute(ReviewCommand: approve, versionBeingReviewed=1)
    Review->>Repo: load(campaignId)
    Repo-->>Review: Campaign(currentVersion=2)
    Review->>Review: compare 1 vs 2 -> mismatch
    Review-->>Reviewer: Err(StaleReviewError(attempted=1, current=2))
    Note over Reviewer: UI: "This campaign has changed since you opened it - please review the latest version."
